  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strategic integration for Sustainable Polder Development: Aligning proposals and perspectives in Bangladesh-the Netherlands collaboration</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The assignment entails facilitating collaboration between the Netherlands and Bangladesh for the enhancement of polder infrastructure operation &amp; maintenance (O&amp;M) and in-polder water management, specifically focusing on the Polder of the Future initiative.The Bangladesh Water Development Board (BWDB) seeks alignment between proposals from the Centre for Environmental and Geographic Information Services (CEGIS) and the Institute of Water Modelling (IWM) with BWDB&apos;s action perspectives.Key tasks include understanding stakeholder plans, developing an outlook for in-polder water management in Bangladesh, connecting with related initiatives, and providing guidance on project arrangements.The timeline spans initial discussions, a joint field visit, and meetings with IWM/CEGIS in February 2024, with expected deliverables including supported outlooks, specific comments on project arrangements, a detailed proposal and a learning agenda plan.The estimated costs encompass the time commitment of key personnel and support, covering preparation, travel, and reporting/presentation.</narrative>
  </description>
